  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(¬R⇒S)≡¬(¬(¬R)∨S).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬R)∨S)≡¬(R∨S).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(R∨S)≡¬R∧¬S\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬R∧¬S.$",
